{
  "cell": "ro_ring5",
  "_comment": [
    "ro_ring5 -- design/ro_array_core.spice's `.subckt ro_ring5 en ro vddr vss`,",
    "composed from the already-committed, individually DRC/LVS-clean leaf cells",
    "layout/ro_nand2/ (xg) and layout/ro_stage/ (x1-x4) at wstv=0.42 (ring 1).",
    "See layout/ro_ring5/README.md for the derivation of every number below.",
    "Four stages, because the ring needs three physical routing planes:",
    "  place  -- placement only, no routing. Origins are pitched so that the",
    "            widest inter-cell nwell gap clears nwell.space.1 (1.27 um):",
    "            g's own nwell ends at local x=5.57 and ro_stage's starts at",
    "            local x=-2.19, so g->s1 needs a >=9.03 um origin delta; 9.30",
    "            is used (1.54 um gap). s1->s4 keep the 8.175 um stage pitch",
    "            (1.705 um gap). The bare placement is DRC-clean on its own.",
    "  sig    -- n1..n4 on metal2 (met1) in one shared lane below the cells",
    "            (y=-1.5). The four nets do not overlap in x, so one lane holds",
    "            all four. li1 was tried first and does not work: every leaf",
    "            gate's `a` port sits inside its own device cluster, so an li1",
    "            approach from any side crosses that gate's own S/D pads.",
    "  fb     -- ro (x4.y back into xg.a) on metal2, in its own gen-compose",
    "            call so it does not contend with n1..n4 for the same lane.",
    "            It leaves g at the one spot on net `a` that is not covered by",
    "            ro_nand2's own met1 (local x=4.98 on the a-side PMOS gate pad;",
    "            4.95 and below fail met1.space.1 against ro_nand2's internal",
    "            y-net met1 arm at local x=4.455-4.625), rises outside g's",
    "            bbox at x=6.3 and crosses the ring at y=5.4, above every",
    "            leaf cell's own met1 (highest is ro_nand2's at y=4.585).",
    "  ro_ring5 (final) -- vddr and vss on metal3 (met2), a plane the leaf",
    "            cells leave completely empty. Both rails' ports are declared",
    "            directly on met1 (on each leaf's own internal rail routing:",
    "            vddr's top arm at local y=4.315-4.485, vss's vertical arm at",
    "            local x=0.415-0.585), so metal3's single-hop via-drop rule is",
    "            satisfied without an intermediate promotion stage.",
    "            vddr buses above the cells (y=6.0), vss below (y=-3.0), so",
    "            neither bus crosses the other's per-gate risers."
  ],
